# Foundry
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/lib/
contracts/broadcast/

# Same, if forge is ever run from the repo root by mistake
/out/
/cache/

# Node
node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Circuit artefacts -- all regenerable via `make circuits`
circuits/build/*_js/
circuits/build/*.r1cs
circuits/build/*.sym
circuits/build/*.wasm
circuits/build/*.zkey

# Verification keys are DERIVED from the zkeys, which are not reproducible: `zkey
# contribute` mixes its own randomness even with fixed `-e` entropy (measured), and that
# non-determinism is a security property rather than a defect. So a committed vkey only
# matches the machine that built it. They were committed once, and the result was a third
# of the test suite failing with InvalidProof() on a clean pull -- committed vkeys against
# locally-built zkeys. CI never caught it because CI regenerates both in the same run.
# `make circuits` regenerates these; do not commit them.
circuits/build/*_vkey.json
circuits/build/*_verifier.sol
circuits/build/*_proof.json
# Exception, committed deliberately: padding-exploit.json pins the exact attack that
# `queuePadding` allowed, so PaddingExploit.t.sol can assert it stays unreachable without
# a 4-minute proof regeneration. It holds a commitment, a proof and public signals --
# no nullifier, no secret, nothing spendable.
!circuits/build/padding-exploit.json
circuits/build/*_calldata.json

# Powers-of-tau: 9.5 MB, downloaded on demand by scripts/build.sh
circuits/build/*.ptau

# SECRETS. committee-key.json holds an ElGamal decryption secret. The Phase 0 key
# is a throwaway test key, but never let this pattern become a habit -- in Phase 2
# the equivalent file can decrypt the entire pool.
circuits/build/committee-key.json

# Generated from committee-key.json by scripts/gen_committee_key_circom.mjs. Public
# key only, but it is a build artefact of a gitignored input -- committing it would
# reintroduce the key-drift bug it exists to prevent.
circuits/src/committee_key.circom
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# Generated verifiers are derived from the zkeys, not source of truth
contracts/src/verifiers/*.sol

# Measurement output
circuits/build/gate-*.json

# Real action proofs for the Solidity suite. Regenerable with `make fixtures`, and
# regenerated with fresh randomness every time, so committing it would churn on every
# build while adding nothing -- the vkeys below are the artefact worth pinning.
circuits/build/action-fixtures.json
circuits/build/*_calldata.json

# `make bench` output. Describes this machine's CPU, not the project -- and it is the
# denominator atrum-client divides browser timings by, so it must be re-measured locally
# rather than inherited from whoever committed last.
circuits/build/proving-baseline.json

# Trusted setup ceremony working directory. Intermediate zkeys are passed hand to hand
# between contributors and are never committed -- `bet_encrypted` alone is 10MB and only the
# final key matters. The public record is TRANSCRIPT.md, which pins every hash.
circuits/ceremony/

# OS
.DS_Store

# V2 probe compile artefacts -- regenerable, and build/fee holds a zkey
circuits/build/bind/
circuits/build/fee/
circuits/build/route/
